Changelog Guidelines

Guiding Principles:
- Changelogs are for humans, not machines.
- There should be an entry for every released version.
- The [Unreleased] section is for changes not yet released.
- Versions and sections should be linkable and easily referenced.
- The latest version comes first (reverse chronological order).
- The release date of each version should be displayed.
- Mention whether the project follows Semantic Versioning (SemVer).
- The same types of changes should be grouped together for clarity.
- Keeping this format consistent makes the changelog readable, maintainable, and easy to navigate.

Types of Changes:
- Added - for new features.
- Changed - for changes in existing functionality.
- Deprecated - for features soon to be removed.
- Removed - for now removed features.
- Fixed - for any bug fixes.
- Security - for vulnerabilities and security fixes.

Usage:
- Start with an [Unreleased] section for ongoing development.
- Add a section for each released version with its version number and release date.
